        "original_id": "5aae30e7-62bb-52f9-a035-b68480ee33de",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Margaret Wilson, Edna St. Vincent Millay\n- Roles: American novelist, American poet, playwright\n- Awards: Pulitzer Prize, Pulitzer Prize for Poetry\n- Concepts: feminist activism\n\nFacts:\n- Margaret Wilson was born on January 16, 1882, and was an American novelist.\n- Edna St. Vincent Millay was born on February 22, 1892, and was an American poet and playwright.\n- Edna St. Vincent Millay received the Pulitzer Prize for Poetry in 1923 and was the third woman to win the award for poetry.\n- Margaret Wilson was awarded the 1924 Pulitzer Prize for \"The Able McLaughlins\".\n- Edna St. Vincent Millay was also known for her feminist activism.\n- Edna St. Vincent Millay died on October 19, 1950.\n- Margaret Wilson died on October 6, 1973.",
